r.a:*(SORT_BY_ALIGNMENT(.text) SORT_BY_ALIGNMENT(.text.*))\n *libzephyr.a:*(SORT_BY_ALIGNMENT(.rodata) SORT_BY_ALIGNMENT(.rodata.*))\n *libzephyr.a:*(SORT_BY_ALIGNMENT(.srodata) SORT_BY_ALIGNMENT(.srodata.*))\n                0x80038b6a                        __ilm_flash_end \u003d .\n```````\n                \nIn `CONFIG_LTO\u003dn`, we can see `libdrivers__serial.a` in our assign region with text length, but in `CONFIG_LTO\u003dy`, `libdrivers__serial.a` in our assign region don\u0027t have any bytes, which means nothing will be copied to `ilm_ram` section.\n\nAnd after enabling the RAM code, it can also reduce EC power number from 11.XmW to 9.XmW on kaladin, so we need this CL to be merged.\n\nAfter this CL is merged, we will start to study if there is a possibility to enable CONFIG_LTO and enable RAM code at the same time.",
